BT 1 0 0 1 0 56.8 Tm /F1 9.2 Tf 13.2 TL (A collapsed core combines core and distribution functions, reducing the number of high-end switches and possibly) Tj T* (saving the cost of one distribution/core layer. For example, if six buildings each would otherwise have two distribution) Tj T* (switches and the campus has two core switches, collapsing the layers may remove a separate pair of distribution) Tj T* (devices only if their functions are absorbed by the core; the exact saving depends on the final device count and port) Tj T* (requirements. The saving must be compared with the cost of larger replacement switches and reduced fault isolation.) Tj T* ET
